{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GgD3DcnxH2YdbMAcon9rE9","type":"tool_result","content":"\\section{Conclusion}\nFor one budgeted Kernel SHAP run on a tabular classifier, reproducibility of the top-3 feature set is conditional on the coalition budget: mean agreement with reruns is 0.807 at $4d$ and 0.932 at $16d$ across three held-out datasets and three model families. A diagnostic that reads only the assessed run lowers squared error against always-reliable, constant-0.5 and split-half-gap baselines and against a pairing-permuted control, with positive bootstrap lower bounds, and the sealed evaluation qualified. The conclusion is bounded. The instance-specific gain over the control is 0.0137, most of the gain over the always-reliable baseline survives permutation, rank resolution is moderate (0.58), and neither the contribution of individual components nor results for individual datasets or families were established. The most useful follow-ups follow directly from these gaps: evaluating a budget-only constant and component ablations, reporting per-cell results with two-sided intervals, adding background and retraining variation to the label, and testing a thresholded flagging rule against a stated cost of top-3 errors.\n\n% IMPORTANT: \\clearpage flushes all pending floats before references so that\n% body-page counting excludes reference-only pages.  Do NOT remove.\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\\zref@newlabel{endbody}{\\posx{7104429}\\posy{13279985}}\n95\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18050b94-e857-4c8d-b7a8-a11a5c26f668","uuid":"63467b4b-8ee9-429b-85d9-34194e926223","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:33:09.654Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\section{Conclusion}\nFor one budgeted Kernel SHAP run on a tabular classifier, reproducibility of the top-3 feature set is conditional on the coalition budget: mean agreement with reruns is 0.807 at $4d$ and 0.932 at $16d$ across three held-out datasets and three model families. A diagnostic that reads only the assessed run lowers squared error against always-reliable, constant-0.5 and split-half-gap baselines and against a pairing-permuted control, with positive bootstrap lower bounds, and the sealed evaluation qualified. The conclusion is bounded. The instance-specific gain over the control is 0.0137, most of the gain over the always-reliable baseline survives permutation, rank resolution is moderate (0.58), and neither the contribution of individual components nor results for individual datasets or families were established. The most useful follow-ups follow directly from these gaps: evaluating a budget-only constant and component ablations, reporting per-cell results with two-sided intervals, adding background and retraining variation to the label, and testing a thresholded flagging rule against a stated cost of top-3 errors.\n\n% IMPORTANT: \\clearpage flushes all pending floats before references so that\n% body-page counting excludes reference-only pages.  Do NOT remove.\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\\zref@newlabel{endbody}{\\posx{7104429}\\posy{13279985}}\n95","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
