I added five references to the draft and rewrote only the three paragraphs flagged in the gap memo. No numbers or experimental claims changed.

The earlier retrieval pass had stopped after query 4 and added nothing. I fetched the five references through the OpenAlex API and edited as follows:

- **Instability comparators (Related Work):** I added Visani et al. 2021, which defines stability indices from repeated LIME runs. I also added Slack et al. 2020, which models the uncertainty of LIME and Kernel SHAP explanations. The paragraph now contrasts them with this paper's question: will one run's top-3 set be reproduced by a rerun?
- **Jackknife and shrinkage (Method):** I cited Kott 2001 for the delete-a-group jackknife and Efron & Morris 1973 for the shrinkage-toward-a-prior idea behind the "empirical-Bayes-style" wording.
- **Deployment claim (Introduction):** I softened "a standard way to justify" to "used to explain" and cited Bhatt et al. 2020 for feature attributions being widely deployed. I also reworded "common deployment practice" to "a common practice, which we take as the case of interest".

I cited Slack and Bhatt from memory of the papers, since I only confirmed their titles and authors through the API, so their one-line descriptions are worth a quick check. To stay at the 30-reference cap I removed Grinsztajn 2022 and the "tree ensembles vs. neural models" clause that cited it.

